# `golem/registry`

`ReplaceWithoutHooks` validates all replacement identities before swapping registry/owner maps under one mutex. It queues complete new spawns and removed old IDs without invoking ordinary lifecycle hooks. The host must quiesce gameplay and connections and restore dependent systems before dispatching explicit recovery hooks. Invalid entries preserve the accepted registry and lifecycle queues; no root runtime import belongs here.

**World state:** the **`Entity`** interface (identity, type name, `Position() (x, y float32)`, `IsGlobal() bool`, `FlushUpdate` / `FullUpdate`), a thread-safe **`Registry`** (add/remove/get, `All`, `FlushAll`, `SnapshotAll`, `TickAll`), and **`FlushResult`** (spawns with IDs, deltas with IDs, removed IDs). **Opt-in entity interfaces:** `Ticker` (`Tick(dt)`), `Spawner` (`OnSpawn()`), `Remover` (`OnRemove()`), `PositionWriter` (`SetPosition(x, y float32)`)—the registry dispatches `Ticker`/`Spawner`/`Remover` automatically; `PositionWriter` is type-asserted by the collision step in `golem.Server` to write physics-corrected positions back to entities. `ReplicationDeltaEntity` supports ACK-aware generic deltas; `CompactReplicationDeltaEntity` supports compact datagram state records. Optional `OwnerScopedEntity` (`PublicFullUpdate`, `PublicReplicationMask`) redacts `visibility: owner` fields for non-owner recipients; entities without it keep authoritative payloads for everyone. `FlushAll` / `SnapshotAll` always use authoritative `FullUpdate` (persistence remains unfiltered). `Add`/`AddOwned` call `OnSpawn` on `Spawner` entities after insertion; `AddWithoutSpawn`/`AddOwnedWithoutSpawn` insert without spawning so `golem.Server.CreateEntity` can register colliders before `NotifySpawn`; `DeleteEntity` calls `OnRemove` on `Remover` entities after deletion; `TickAll(dt)` calls `Tick(dt)` on every `Ticker`. All hooks run **outside** the registry mutex so hook code may safely call back into the registry. The registry tracks entity **lifecycle events** between flushes: `Add` records spawns, `DeleteEntity` records despawns. `FlushAll` returns a `FlushResult` with `SpawnIDs`/`Spawns`, `DeltaIDs`/`Deltas`, and `Removals`, then resets the tracking. `All()` returns a snapshot slice of every entity for interest-management grid updates. **Ownership tracking:** `AddOwned(entity, sessionID)` records which session owns an entity; `Owner(entityID)` looks it up; `SetOwner(entityID, sessionID)` transfers ownership (sessionID `0` clears ownership). Game code uses **`golem.Server.CreateEntity(e, sessionID)`** (and `Owner` / `Get` / `SetOwner` on `Server`); the generated **`CommandRouter`** takes `*golem.Server` and calls those methods. The **`golem`** package does not re-export `Registry`; behavior lives here.
